IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `esos-student`
IMPORT `esos-refund`

-- ESOS refund instruments -- worked cases, from the overseas student's seat (REQ-0102). Expected values were worked by hand
-- from the deposited Calculation of Refund Instrument 2024 (with its formulas sidecar), the Suitable Alternative Courses
-- Instrument 2022 and National Code Standard 3, never copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- The student of the ledger's question: a 364-day course with $36,000 of tuition fees; she paid $18,000, covering the first
-- 182 days. Weekly tuition fee: 36000 / 364 x 7 = 692.31, rounded up to $693 (s 6).
#ASSERT `What is my weekly tuition fee` 36000 364 EQUALS 693
-- A fee that comes out whole is not rounded: 36400 / 364 x 7 = 700.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly tuition fee` 36400 364 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `the weeks in default period` 182 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `the weeks in default period` 180 EQUALS 26
#ASSERT `the weeks in default period` 91 EQUALS 13

-- The provider fails to start the course: 182 days of the paid period remain: 26 weeks x $693 = $18,018 -- $18 more than she
-- paid, because both figures are rounded up (NOTES.md finding 20).
#ASSERT `How much must my defaulting provider refund` 36000 364 182 EQUALS 18018
-- The provider stops teaching 91 days in: 13 weeks x $693 = $9,009.
#ASSERT `How much must my defaulting provider refund` 36000 364 91 EQUALS 9009

-- She withdraws with 70 days of the paid period left and no compliant written agreement: 10 x $693 = $6,930 (s 9).
#ASSERT `How much must my provider refund under s 47E` `the provider never entered into a written agreement with me that meets s 47B` 36000 364 70 18000 0 EQUALS 6930
-- Her visa is refused and she never starts: course fees $18,000 + $500 non-tuition = $18,500; 5% is $925, so $500 is
-- deducted: $18,000 (s 10(2)).
#ASSERT `How much must my provider refund under s 47E` `my student visa was refused, so I did not start the course on the agreed day` 36000 364 182 18000 500 EQUALS 18000
-- A smaller payment of $6,000: 5% is $300, less than $500: $5,700.
#ASSERT `How much must my provider refund under s 47E` `my student visa was refused, so I did not start the course on the agreed day` 36000 364 182 6000 0 EQUALS 5700
-- Visa refused after starting, so she withdraws with 91 days paid ahead: the weekly formula (s 10(4)): $9,009.
#ASSERT `How much must my provider refund under s 47E` `my student visa was refused, so I withdrew or did not pay` 36000 364 91 18000 0 EQUALS 9009

-- National Code Standard 3.
#ASSERT `Does my agreement meet the national code` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my agreement meet the national code` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does my agreement meet the national code` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Default day 1 February 2027, compliant agreement, claim received 10 February: under the agreement by 10 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What refund after my default under the national code` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 2 2027) EQUALS `a refund of the amount my written agreement sets, to me or the person it names, within 4 weeks after my written claim: by` (Date 10 3 2027)
-- The agreement lacks the refund information: s 47E, by 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What refund after my default under the national code` (Date 1 2 2027) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 10 2 2027) EQUALS `a refund of the amount the Minister's instrument sets, to me, within 4 weeks after the default day: by` (Date 1 3 2027)

-- Suitable alternative course criteria.
#ASSERT `Do the criteria point to a suitable alternative course` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `every criterion points to it being suitable: registered (or arranged) provider, similar level and field, a workable location, and acceptable to me`
#ASSERT `Do the criteria point to a suitable alternative course` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not every criterion points to it; the TPS Director weighs them (Suitable Alternative Courses Instrument s 6)`

-- The duties as rules. Agreement made at the moment of payment: FULFILLED. A day after: BREACH.
#TRACE `the agreement-before-payment duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `enter into a written agreement with me` AT 0
#TRACE `the agreement-before-payment duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `enter into a written agreement with me` AT 1
-- New address notified 5 days after moving: FULFILLED. Refund paid 30 days after the default day: BREACH.
#TRACE `my contact details duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the student` DOES `tell my provider my new contact details` AT 5
#TRACE `the s 47E refund duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my provider` DOES `pay my refund` AT 30
